.page seq 1 print a sequence of numbers

# SYNOPSIS
*seq* _LAST_
*seq* _FIRST_ _LAST_
*seq* _FIRST_ _STEP_ _LAST_

# DESCRIPTION
`seq` prints the numbers from _FIRST_ (default 1) to _LAST_, one per line, going up or down by _STEP_ (default 1). If _FIRST_ and _STEP_ are whole numbers the output is whole numbers; otherwise numbers are printed in the shortest `%g` form. A _STEP_ of zero, or the wrong number of arguments, is an error.

# EXAMPLES
    seq 5
    seq 10 -3 0
    seq 0 0.25 1
    for i in $(seq 1 3); do echo "round $i"; done

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 for bad arguments.

# SEE ALSO
expr(1), shuf(1), gapsh-language(7)
